message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Code and aggregated results for two-stage and direct supplier price forecasting"
type: software
version: v1.0.0
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23484546
date-released: 2026-11-23
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Royo
    given-names: Beatriz
    affiliation: "Fundación Zaragoza Logistics Center (ZLC)"
  - family-names: "de la Cruz Eiriz"
    given-names: "María Teresa"
    affiliation: "Fundación Zaragoza Logistics Center (ZLC)"
abstract: "Python implementation of a two-stage forecasting framework (upstream commodity prices to supplier prices) and direct baselines (SARIMAX, XGBoost with exogenous variables), evaluated with rolling-origin multi-horizon forecasting, bootstrap prediction intervals, Diebold-Mariano tests and a decision-oriented threshold-crossing evaluation. The proprietary supplier series is not included; only the expected input format is provided."
keywords:
  - supplier price forecasting
  - two-stage forecasting
  - rolling-origin evaluation
  - SARIMAX
  - XGBoost
  - procurement
